# .gitignore for the Surgery Advisor
#
# A .gitignore only stops untracked files from being added. It does not
# remove files that are already committed, and it does not catch a secret
# pasted into a tracked file. The pre-commit secret scan (see AGENTS.md,
# "Secrets") covers those cases.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and credentials. This project needs none; if one ever appears,
# it goes in .env (ignored) and its name, never its value, in .env.example.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.env
.envrc
secrets/
.secrets/
*.secret
*.secrets
credentials*.json
service-account*.json
client_secret*.json
token*.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.kdbx
id_rsa*
id_dsa*
id_ecdsa*
id_ed25519*
.netrc
.pypirc
.npmrc
.git-credentials

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project output: benchmark reports and decision logs can be large and may
# contain local paths.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
reports/
logs/
*.jsonl
scratch/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python and tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Personal agent and editor settings (shared ones like CLAUDE.md and
# .claude/settings.json stay tracked)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/settings.local.json
.aider*
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operating system files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini